{"team":"NYG","col":"#5C8FF0","identity":"balanced","funnel":"run-funnel","plays_pg":62.6,"adot":7.6,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>A Balanced Attack</h2><p>There's no bell-cow to bank on \u2014 the lead back sees just <strong>50%</strong> of carries (league ~59%), a committee that caps any one back's ceiling and makes their rushing props matchup- and script-dependent.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>In the passing game the ball funnels to <strong>Malik Nabers</strong> \u2014 <strong>29% of targets</strong> (league ~23%), a genuine alpha share that concentrates the receiving value at the top.</p><p>They run downhill \u2014 mostly inside the tackles (18% to the edge vs ~25%), a gap/power scheme that trades big plays for a steady, grinding floor.</p><p>The WR2 is unusually involved here \u2014 <strong>19%</strong> of targets (league ~15%), meaning there's bankable volume beyond the top receiver.</p><p>They lean on tempo \u2014 a 17% no-huddle rate (league ~11%) that inflates snap counts and everyone's volume.</p><p>The tight end is barely used in the passing game (11% of targets vs ~15%) \u2014 fade their TE's receiving props.</p><p>By the numbers it's a struggling unit \u2014 a 41% success rate (below the 44% average).</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Inside the 20 they lean run-heavy, passing <strong>50%</strong> of the time, funnelling touchdown equity to <strong>Tyrone Tracy Jr.</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 The Run Comes Free</h2><p>They surrender <strong>142 rushing</strong> and <strong>229 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). The run moves against them \u2014 <strong>target opposing RB1s</strong>.</p><p>They lock down opposing tight ends \u2014 just 26 rec yds/game (vs ~35); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They lock down opposing WR1s \u2014 just 53 rec yds/game (vs ~58); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They lock down opposing WR2s \u2014 just 32 rec yds/game (vs ~36); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They leak <strong>RB rushing TDs</strong> (0.53/game vs ~0.46) \u2014 an anytime-TD spot to attack.</p><p>Broadly a leaky unit \u2014 46% success rate allowed (vs ~44%); points come easy against them.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: <strong>opposing RB1s</strong> smash on the ground and at the goal line.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Jaxson Dart","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":29,"props":{"Comp":18.9,"Att":29.0,"Pass Yds":198.99,"Pass TD":1.46,"INT":1.09,"Rush Yds":17.74},"d":{"completions":18.9,"attempts":29.0,"pass_yards":198.99,"pass_td":1.46,"interceptions":1.09,"rush_att":3.15,"rush_yards":17.74}}],"RB":[{"name":"Cam Skattebo","slot":"RB1","starter":true,"td":46,"props":{"Rush Att":13.03,"Rush Yds":54.52,"Tgt":5.03,"Rec":3.97,"Rec Yds":31.37},"d":{"rush_att":13.03,"rush_yards":54.52,"targets":5.03,"receptions":3.97,"rec_yards":31.37,"rec_td":0.14}},{"name":"Najee Harris","slot":"RB2","starter":true,"td":19,"props":{"Rush Att":4.17,"Rush Yds":16.29,"Tgt":3.06,"Rec":2.04,"Rec Yds":13.31},"d":{"rush_att":4.17,"rush_yards":16.29,"targets":3.06,"receptions":2.04,"rec_yards":13.31,"rec_td":0.06}},{"name":"Tyrone Tracy Jr.","slot":"RB3","starter":false,"td":27,"props":{"Rush Att":13.36,"Rush Yds":58.49,"Tgt":4.98,"Rec":3.75,"Rec Yds":28.55},"d":{"rush_att":13.36,"rush_yards":58.49,"targets":4.98,"receptions":3.75,"rec_yards":28.55,"rec_td":0.1}},{"name":"Devin Singletary","slot":"RB4","starter":false,"td":24,"props":{"Rush Att":5.21,"Rush Yds":22.33,"Tgt":3.15,"Rec":2.17,"Rec Yds":14.03},"d":{"rush_att":5.21,"rush_yards":22.33,"targets":3.15,"receptions":2.17,"rec_yards":14.03,"rec_td":0.04}}],"WR":[{"name":"Malik Nabers","slot":"WR1","starter":true,"td":27,"props":{"Tgt":10.04,"Rec":6.37,"Rec Yds":74.53,"Rec TD":0.32},"d":{"targets":10.04,"receptions":6.37,"rec_yards":74.53,"rec_td":0.32}},{"name":"Malachi Fields","slot":"WR2","st